WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:03.470
Here's how to get set up with
TritonAI Harness, from your

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.720
access request to your first
response.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:06.840
It takes five steps.

00:00:07.703 --> 00:00:08.963
Step one.

00:00:08.963 --> 00:00:12.543
On the TritonAI website, open
Build, then Get Started.

00:00:12.543 --> 00:00:16.383
Under Get your access key,
select Request Gateway Access,

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.993
and sign in with your UC San
Diego account.

00:00:20.203 --> 00:00:22.073
This is the request form.

00:00:22.303 --> 00:00:26.073
The first question asks whether your
work involves UC Health data.

00:00:26.283 --> 00:00:28.593
For campus administrative work, choose No.

00:00:30.237 --> 00:00:32.577
Next, choose your requester type.

00:00:32.577 --> 00:00:36.837
For everyday administrative work, pick
Individual, Default Allocation.

00:00:36.837 --> 00:00:39.277
It uses the models hosted
at UC San Diego, and

00:00:39.277 --> 00:00:40.987
there's no recharge for
that work.

00:00:42.437 --> 00:00:45.637
If you need cloud models,
like GPT, Claude, or

00:00:45.637 --> 00:00:48.607
Gemini, choose Extended
Access instead.

00:00:48.677 --> 00:00:52.517
Cloud models are charged from the
first token, so the form asks for the

00:00:52.517 --> 00:00:55.467
project and task to charge, which is
your chartstring.

00:00:55.757 --> 00:00:57.907
Grant-funded research works differently:

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.777
hosted and cloud models are both
charged to the grant.

00:01:00.777 --> 00:01:04.647
You can check current models and rates
in the TritonAI model catalog.

00:01:04.737 --> 00:01:07.427
For this example, we'll keep
the default allocation.

00:01:08.903 --> 00:01:11.613
Your name and email are filled in for you.

00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:12.833
We've hidden them here.

00:01:13.103 --> 00:01:15.733
Open the Department list, and
choose your department.

00:01:17.337 --> 00:01:20.707
Then describe what you plan to
do, in a sentence or two.

00:01:20.877 --> 00:01:22.587
Be specific about the work.

00:01:22.737 --> 00:01:23.527
For example:

00:01:23.677 --> 00:01:27.737
Use TritonAI Harness to draft
training guides, summarize meeting

00:01:27.737 --> 00:01:30.907
notes, and prepare reports for
department operations.

00:01:32.603 --> 00:01:35.113
Scroll down to the data protection levels.

00:01:35.363 --> 00:01:37.473
Levels 1 through 3 are approved.

00:01:37.683 --> 00:01:40.573
Level 4, restricted or
health data, is not.

00:01:40.923 --> 00:01:42.453
Check the box to acknowledge that.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.250
Review your answers, then select Submit.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.820
For the models hosted at UC San Diego,
approval is automatic,

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.910
and your key link is emailed right away.

00:01:52.103 --> 00:01:53.303
Step two.

00:01:53.303 --> 00:01:57.283
When your access is ready, you'll get
an email with a one-time link.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.213
The key itself isn't in the email.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.810
Open the link, copy your
key, and save it somewhere

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.040
secure before you leave the
page.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.140
Treat it like a password.

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:09.870
Step three.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:13.630
Back on Get Started, download
the stable installer.

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:18.470
On an Apple silicon Mac, open the DMG
and launch TritonAI Installer.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.340
On Windows, run the setup file.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:22.970
Step four.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.790
Paste your key, then select
Check access and install.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.960
Keep the installer open until it finishes.

00:02:30.537 --> 00:02:31.777
Step five.

00:02:31.777 --> 00:02:33.637
Open TritonAI Harness.

00:02:33.637 --> 00:02:37.497
Before you send anything, set
the mode to Supervised, so

00:02:37.497 --> 00:02:39.717
file changes wait for your
approval.

00:02:39.717 --> 00:02:41.697
Then type a simple request, like:

00:02:41.697 --> 00:02:43.887
Help me outline a meeting agenda.

00:02:46.137 --> 00:02:48.687
When you get a response, you're set up.

00:02:48.837 --> 00:02:51.047
Review it the way you'd review any draft.

00:02:52.737 --> 00:02:57.507
To keep going, try the Harness Essentials
course on the TritonAI website.

